## Decisions taken (user, 2026-09-02, after the cross-vendor BLOCK review)

- **O-1 → HOLD the incumbent constraint set, measure at G0-C.** The incumbent IS a ConstraintTRPO
  (IPO log-barrier) teacher: `joint1_position_cost`, `cumulative_yaw_cost`, `thruster_utilization_cost`
  etc. are threshold rules optimized through a barrier (`constraints.py`, `constraint_trpo.py:surrogate`),
  so training is not constraint-free. Decision: keep all 10 UNCHANGED for attributability. This program
  adds no NEW shaping and STRENGTHENS nothing (an earlier draft's "raise the J1 penalty" lever is removed
  — no such knob exists and it would violate constraint 1).
- **O-2 → OPEN BY DESIGN, contingent on G0-C.** `thruster_util` is already 0.82–0.93 of its 0.40 budget
  on the healthy plant; with more fault mass the survivors must work harder, so the barrier penalizes
  exactly the thrust FTC needs and can teach thrust UNDER-use — the opposite of the goal. G0-C measures
  the margin as a PRIMARY readout. If it binds, that is a new decision (accept an FTC ceiling vs. change
  the budget, which is itself shaping and cost −54 % reward when halved, `finding/052`) — escalate, never
  silently retune. This is the one issue deliberately left unresolved until measured.
- **O-3 → GENERALIZED fault DR (B-family), NOT special mass on the deployed pattern.** The user rejected
  option C: putting explicit weight on `(m3,m4)` specializes the policy for the broken robot, which is
  the framing they already rejected once ("논문 쓸 때 로봇 고장났다고 말할 거냐"). So the strengthening is
  **uniform over all six channels with no pair awareness** — `(m3,m4)` is one naturally-occurring
  double-loss sample, not a weighted case. Spec in Phase 1; the deployed pattern's coverage is therefore
  DILUTED by construction, and Phase 4 keeps the real pair as the PRIMARY exam so a generalization
  failure is caught rather than assumed away.
- **O-4 → FINAL teacher trains on the WORKSTATION; ksm-nas (DGX) does screening / parallel-seed only.**
  The +109 % cross-machine term is a same-seed/same-config pair — the actual machine-isolation
  comparison — so cross-seed variance does not erase it, and one-machine re-scoring fixes only
  eval-machine variance. **Recorded departure from the Objective:** the user's verbatim goal says
  "ksm-nas 에서 ... 재학습 수행"; this decision (made later, with the machine-isolation evidence in front
  of the user) moves the FINAL deployed teacher to the workstation. Noted explicitly so the change is
  visible, not silent; ksm-nas keeps the screening/probe role the objective also assigns it.

