## What this program is, and what it is not

It IS: one teacher retrain that makes actuator faults a DISTRIBUTION the policy must absorb (single AND
double loss, complete death, vertical channels — the real m3-dead / m4-excluded state is ONE sample of
that distribution), applies the ≈1-step ACTION latency, and corrects the over-estimated vertical-TAM
pitch moment — with every OTHER knob held at the incumbent's as-run value so the result is
attributable. It is NOT a plant with the thrusters glued off (the user rejected that axis twice); the
fixed-health vectors are EVAL instruments, never a training plant. It is NOT plant-v2 (hydro/added-mass/
thrust-curve corrections, `decision/209`) — those stay gated on bench measurements that do not exist;
it is NOT a reward or constraint redesign. It adds NO NEW hard clamp, latch, or rule-based shaping to
training. Honest caveat (O-1): the incumbent already IS a ConstraintTRPO teacher with 10 IPO barrier
constraints — this program keeps that set UNCHANGED for attributability and does NOT strengthen any of
them (an earlier draft's "raise the J1 penalty" lever is removed — it would be new shaping and no such
weight knob exists). Whether the incumbent's barrier formulation itself should change is O-1, a user
decision, not a silent edit. Robot-damage prevention stays where it already is — deployment-side guards
(`joint_current_max_ma` 1000–1200, `start_att_max_deg` 45, J1 cable-wrap rail 6π, J2>π abort,
`launch_driver:=false`) — and none of them enters the training environment.

